   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the county of Orleans to offer an optional twenty year\nretirement plan to Kevin Colonna, a deputy sheriff employed by such county",
    "basePrintNo": "S3722",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3722-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3722\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the county of  Orleans to offer an optional twenty\nyear retirement plan to Kevin Colonna, a deputy sheriff employed by such\ncounty\n\n \nPURPOSE: OF THE BILL:\n\nThis legislation will authorize Officer Kevin Colonna, of the Orleans\nCounty Sheriffs Office, to transfer a defined period of service credit\nhe accrued under Section 89L to Section 553.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 transfers Mr. Colonna's service time under Section 89L to\nsection 553 if the County of Orleans elects to assume any additional\ncosts.\n\nSection 2 clarifies that Mr. Colonna must formally request this change\nto the State Comptroller within 18 months of the effective date.\n\nSection 3 clarifies that all costs associated with this change are borne\nby his employer.\n\nSection 4 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor reasons not ascribable to his own negligence, Mr. Colonna was previ-\nously enrolled in Section 89L instead of Section 553. This bill places\nhim in the proper system.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: Referred to Rules.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe bill would take effect immediately.\n",
